      "title": "Reporting is becoming a live data feed",
      "text": "Romania's ONJN, rebuilding after the early-2025 discovery that more than EUR900m in taxes was missing from its records, has worked with the country's Digital Authority to build a real-time metadata analysis system for detecting suspicious transactions, alongside probes into suspected GGR manipulation by online operators and audits of five fiscal years of land-based declarations. Regulator boss Vlad-Cristian Soare also launched a fully digital self-exclusion tool, with an Emergency Ordinance proposed to force its rollout across online operators. Both of those are platform requirements dressed as regulatory reform. Real-time monitoring means the reporting obligation is a continuous, reconcilable stream rather than a periodic return, and a mandated digital self-exclusion register means a cross-operator exclusion check in the account and session path. Markets that go this way tend not to go back, so treating regulatory reporting reliability as a first-class SLA rather than a back-office batch job is the safer default.",
