    "expanded": "Written by Viktor Kayed. Hoffstedt said: \"It is tricky that the government, in addition to proposing new laws on the gambling market and through its authority supervising the gambling market, also runs its own commercial gambling company... I hope that the state sells its commercial gambling company and instead focuses on its unique role... I also hope that the entire gambling market is then reregulated, so that competition is also allowed into the lottery market.\" He said the government \"has not taken a single measure to increase the attractiveness of the national gambling license market during the current term of office, which ends this autumn when the Swedish people go to the polls again,\" and called the dual-track strategy \"doomed to fail.\" He noted Sweden has \"the highest proportion of online gambling in all of Europe with just over 68%,\" against a channelisation rate that has fallen to 84%. On Finland's 2027 liberalisation he said: \"If Finland does like Sweden and Denmark but skips our most embarrassing mistakes, Finland will become a beacon of light in Europe in gambling regulation.\" SBC Summit Lisbon runs from 29 September to 1 October.",
