    "expanded": "Written by Sam McQuillan. Most beta activity came after 13 August, per exchange data from TickerTracker. US sports contracts account for more than 99% of Polymarket's $15.5bn of 2026 trading volume. The beta product, not yet broadly available on app or desktop, allows between two and ten legs bundled into a single $1 position, all of which must settle favourably to pay out; Polymarket filed it with the CFTC in May as \"Combinatorial Athletic Outcome Contracts\" and self-certified on 20 May. Pricing runs through a request-for-quote system with market makers. Parlays produce hold rates roughly four times higher than straight bets, and more than 70% of NFL and NBA bets placed with FanDuel in 2025 were parlays. At Kalshi, parlays reported under its \"Exotics\" category overtook traditional sports contracts to lead weekly volume from the week of 2 August. DraftKings plans to invest up to $300m in prediction markets and Flutter has targeted up to $300m for FanDuel Predicts. Polymarket US operates through QCX, a CFTC-designated contract market. Kentucky, Wisconsin and New York have sued prediction markets, and the CFTC has sued states seeking to restrict the exchanges.",
