    "meta": "Yogonet | 19 Aug 2026",
    "summary": "Aggregator Infingame and distributor 3 Oaks Gaming set out the case for regionalising content and mechanics across Latin America, Africa and Eastern Europe, citing differences in volatility preference, session length, tournament participation and game discovery.",
    "why": "If preferred volatility, promotional frequency and tournament mechanics vary by region, then lobby ranking, tournament templates and bonus defaults need to be market-scoped configuration rather than global defaults, and most portfolios are still shipped globally.",
    "expanded": "Lasse Hjelm Mathiasen, head of account management at Infingame, said: \"The era of building the same casino for every market is over,\" and \"Operators that understand how players behave in each region consistently achieve stronger engagement than those relying on identical portfolios across multiple jurisdictions.\" Cited regional differences include preferred volatility profiles, session duration, tournament participation, reaction to gamification, promotional frequency, game discovery, mobile versus desktop usage and engagement with live casino, crash and instant games. European operators are described as optimising for long-term retention and behavioural segmentation, while Latin American operators use tournaments more aggressively for acquisition, with simpler mechanics such as Bet Race and Win Race outperforming complex structures. Mathiasen concluded: \"The most successful operators no longer ask which games are popular globally... They ask which games perform best for their players, in their market, under their commercial strategy... Success isn't built on offering every game available. It's built on delivering the right games, to the right audience, at the right time.\" Federico Miele, head of account management at 3 Oaks Gaming, said: \"Regional preferences have become a key consideration throughout the game development process... By working closely with aggregation partners like Infingame, we gain valuable market insights that help us deliver content with stronger local relevance and long-term player engagement.\"",
